  "note": "The anatomical comparison is strongest with Akkadian luʾu. The Aramaic forms denote the neighboring jaw or cheek. The catalogue indexes Obadiah 1:16 and Job 6:3 under both verbs. Drinking in Obadiah and Job’s explicit reference to his words guide the assignments here. The derivation of the speech verb remains uncertain."
